cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use biosqi in research, please cite this software."
title: "biosqi: Transparent biomedical signal-quality assessment"
abstract: >-
  biosqi is an open-source Python toolkit for explainable, calibrated
  signal-quality assessment of ECG, PPG, and EEG recordings. It produces
  window-aligned quality scores, sample-level masks, and per-window evidence
  attributing poor quality to mains interference, baseline wander, clipping,
  dropout, abnormal amplitude, or poor beat consistency.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Akshaj"
    family-names: "Bachu"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-22
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/akshajbachu/biosqi"
url: "https://akshajbachu.github.io/biosqi"
keywords:
  - biomedical signal processing
  - signal quality index
  - ECG
  - PPG
  - EEG
  - explainability
